# Lane o544_review: independent review of the official VSI-Bench read kit for the step-544 model (read-only; try to break it)

## What is being reviewed
A GPT-family lane built a kit that reads a 9B spatial vision-language model (training step 544) on the official VSI-Bench (5,130 questions) with the same reader as an accepted development-set read; only the item set, the frames and an admission and scoring wrapper are new. Read \`$R/official544/BRIEF.md\`, \`$R/official544/events/20261115T0620Z_RESULT_direct_arm.md\` (whole), \`$R/official544/STATUS.md\`, the kit under \`$R/official544\` (find \`kit/\`, \`out/DEPLOYMENT.json\`, \`out/SITE_EVIDENCE.json\`, \`out/FINAL_CPU_VERIFICATION.json\`, the coverage and pin tables its RESULT names). One H100 on another cluster will run it for an estimated 3 to 5 hours, so a fault found after launch costs that much. You are a different model family.

## Questions, in order of value
1. **Will the job run to a score?** Read the launch path end to end (\`kit/PREPARE.sh\`, \`kit/RUN.sh\` and the Python entrypoints they call: staging, model identity gate, the 20 first-item layout probes, generation, budget journals, extraction, scoring, report). List every line the GPU job executes that the CPU rehearsal did not, from the coverage data, and check each statically (names, argument order, keys, shapes, paths that exist only on one machine, environment variables). Where one file is pinned in several places, show whether all copies agree.
2. **Is the protocol really the accepted one?** Check the claim that the 36 reader source entries are byte-identical to the accepted read, and that frame count and layout (32 anchors, each repeated: 64 inputs), timing, pixel budget, decoding, thinking setting and budgets are unchanged. An earlier loss of 3 to 13 points came from an evaluation frame layout that differed from training. Does the layout probe compare against the accepted layout on real pixels before any item is scored, and does a mismatch stop the job?
3. **Scoring.** Does the wrapper reproduce the recorded official scores of the two reference models from their existing answer files (the lane says nine unit tests do)? Is the aggregation the official one (eight tasks, direction's three subtypes averaged first), the bootstrap paired by scene (288 scenes, 10,000 draws, seed 17)?
4. **Routed types.** This model answers absolute distance (834 items) and room size (288 items) by writing tool calls, and this kit serves no tools. What does the kit do when the model emits a call: stop at the first call, let it run to the token cap, or parse a number from it? What does the report then print for those two tasks and for the overall score? The report must give the six direct tasks as the result, mark the two routed tasks as unserved-call artifacts with their call rate, and must not print an eight-task overall as if it were comparable. Say what it does today and the smallest change if it differs. Also estimate the GPU time those 1,122 items would waste if each runs to the cap, and whether stopping at the first call is safe.
5. **Labels.** Do official answers enter any file the generation step reads? They must reach only the scorer after generation closes.
6. Anything else likely to waste the allocation (time limit against the 3 to 5 hour estimate, disk on the node, resume after a kill, what is lost if the job is killed at hour 3).

## Rules
- Read-only everywhere except your lane folder. No GPU, no launch, no ssh, no agents, no Git commands. Python: \`/scratch/jjyeung/envs/p1cpu/bin/python -I -s -B\`, at most 8 threads; scripts under \`work/\`; lane under 500 MB.
- Never list or search \`/home\` or \`/data*\`. No recursive search outside \`$R/official544\`, \`$R/official_reads\`, \`$R/evalx/work/milestone/reports\` and \`$R/evalx/work/o5130\`. Do not open the official answer fields except through the kit's own scorer tests.
- No deletion commands, and no names of deletion operations in shell command text. Never read a file over 20 MB whole.
- Time box: about 45 minutes.

## Deliver
\`out/REVIEW_VERDICT_OFFICIAL544.md\`: verdict on the first line (\`LAUNCH\`, \`LAUNCH AFTER FIXES\` or \`DO NOT LAUNCH\`), findings ranked by how likely each is to waste the allocation, each with file:line, evidence and the smallest fix; the answer to question 4 in its own section; what you did not check. One event \`events/<stamp>_RESULT_review.md\` (stamp from \`date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%MZ\` in the writing command), at most 30 lines. Then stay alive 20 minutes checking \`inbox/\` once a minute, and end.
